    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1055">

                <pb facs="0912" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg796"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/14726a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Johnson</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You are instructed to deliver a most earnest warning to the commanders of both
                    factions carrying on warfare about Matamoros that they must conduct their
                    operations at Matamoros in such manner as not to menace the lives of American
                    citizens at Brownsville by firing across the border. Telegraph results
                    representations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
